# Milestone: v0.10.11-channel-and-isA
# Covers: exception regressions: uninitialized var += in catch; asString exception
#         in asTopLevelPrintable; 1:1 non-tag colon error; scheduler stuck on
#         concurrent throw + freeze scenario.
# blocked: compound-assign / bare-catch / named-function-decl (defer-v1.x)
# matrix-row: exceptions-try-catch
#
# Reason:
#   Exception structured-throw now works (v0.11.4-cat-f: catchable typed
#   instances, isA() guards, !!! <message> uncaught diagnostic — see
#   exceptions.chk).  These four legacy regression cases are blocked on
#   OTHER still-unsupported surface, not structured-throw:
#     1. `var test; try { test += 3 } catch { ... }` — needs both `+=`
#        compound assignment AND bare `catch {` (no `(var e)`); both
#        unsupported (parser: `+=` -> "unexpected token"; `catch {` ->
#        "expected '('").
#     2. `class X { function asString () { 0/0 } }` — named-function
#        declarations are unsupported at v1.0 ("use 'var name = function...'").
#     3. `1:1` non-tag colon — our parser emits a different diagnostic
#        than the legacy "expected a Tag" message.
#     4. scheduler-stuck (concurrent throw + `t.freeze`) — also needs bare
#        `catch`.
#   Activate when `+=` / bare-catch / named-function-decls land (v1.x).
#
# Original urbiscript (activate when Exception structured-throw lands):
# # var test; try { test += 3 } catch { test = 1; test += 3 };
# # [00000001] 4
# # echo(test); [00000002] *** 4
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/exceptions/regressions.chk)
